-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",157,{
[4993]="700006E7\n1\tDefeat Gloomleaf\tGloomleaf can be found in the north-west of Agamaur. Radagast the Brown has tasked you with destroying the corrupted creatures of Agamaur in an effort to cleanse the Gaunt-lord Ivar's evil from the swamp. In your absence, he learned of a great Huorn that was corrupted and is the force stirring the other Huorns. He has asked you to destroy Gloomleaf.\n2\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast is in the Eglain camp in the southern reaches of Agamaur, near the entrance. Radagast sent you to destroy the great Huorn Gloomleaf in an effort to cleanse Ivar's evil from Agamaur. The deed done, it is time to return to Radagast with the tragic news of your success.\n",
[4994]="70027B5A\n1\tFind Braigiar's body, and Théodred will carry it back to the encampment\tBraigiar's body is in the centre of the village of Tûr Morva, where he fell during his escape with Radanir. Radanir has asked you to recover Braigiar's body from the centre of Tûr Morva.\n2\tTalk to Radanir at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras\tRadanir is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras. Radanir will be pleased to know that you have recovered Braigiar's body.\n",
[4995]="70054039\n1\tDefeat Elf-wights (total: 5)\030Defeat fallen soldier wights (total: 5)\tElf-wights and fallen soldier wights can be found in Parth Daenath. You should lay to rest your slain fellows.\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found at Echad-in-Edhil. You should talk to Thranduil.\n",
[4996]="7002D082\n1\tTalk to Ordhrien\tErymeldir claims to know little of the ancient Elvish ruins within the Limlight Gorge, saying that they were abandoned even before he was born He suggested that you may want to ask Ordhrien about them as she is a good bit older than he.\n",
[4997]="7005A997\n1\tRecover supplies (total: 10)\tSupplies can be found in northern Máttugard. You should recover supplies.\n2\tBring the supplies to Dargumë\tDargumë can be found at Asbaj-khîrfin. You should bring the supplies to Dargumë.\n",
[4998]="7003EB04\n1\tDefeat Huorns in the North Trollshaws (total: 6)\tHuorns can be found in the Gladdalf, in the North Trollshaws. Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to put down the Huorns of the North Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is posted to the south and west of the Gladdalf in the North Trollshaws. You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.\n",
[4999]="70053398\n1\tDefeat maddened marsh-lurkers in the Gladden Fields (total: 14)\tMaddened marsh-lurkers can be found at Gilvamyr and Gladden Falls in the Gladden Fields. A few may also be found wandering the Gladden Fields. You have encountered a number of maddened marsh-lurkers stalking the Gladden Fields. You must defeat them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many maddened marsh-lurkers in the Gladden Fields.\n",
[5000]="7000817E\n1\tCollect bones from the bone-piles (total: 3)\tA large pack of Wargs has moved into northern Annúndir, and the bones of their kills litter the burial mounds in the north. Orthonn is concerned that a small traveller did not make it safely to Amon Raith, and has asked you to search Haudh Eglain for any sign of problems.\n2\tTalk to Orthonn\030Collect Gnawed Bones (total: 3)\tOrthonn is at Ost Lagoros, on the eastern edge of Annúndir. You should speak with Orthonn.\n",
[5001]="7000F236\n1\tBring the banner to Reginald Ward's herald\030Collect the banner\tReginald Ward's banner is lost in one of the encampments of the Angmarim on the ice-shelf, south-east of Sûri-kylä. Reginald's herald has asked you to retrieve his Captain's banner, which he lost during the attack by the Angmarim.\n2\tTell Reginald Ward where his wayward herald can be found\tReginald Ward is at Sûri-kylä, north-west of the ice-shelf. Reginald Ward's herald has asked you to tell his Captain that he is safe and where he can be found.\n",
[5002]="70035836\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Fallows (total: 10)\tThe forces of Isengard can be found in the Fallows. You should ride to the Fallows and defeat the enemies of Wildermore.\n2\tReturn to Ealswith\tEalswith is in Forlaw. You should return to Ealswith.\n",
[5003]="70035855\n1\tCollect the sickle\030Collect the hoe\030Collect the sacks of supplies\tThe hoe, sickle, and sacks of supplies can be found at the farmsteads in the southern Fallows. You should ride to the Fallows and gather the requested supplies.\n2\tReturn to Ealswith\tEalswith is in Forlaw. You should return to Ealswith.\n",
[5004]="700083A5\n1\tPlant false orders (quantity: see journal)\tStrongboxes can be found throughout the city of Dûn Covád, in the western hills north of Fail-á-Khro. Soltakh has asked you to slip false orders into the strongboxes used by the Angmarim chain of command for communication of tasks.\n2\tTalk to Soltakh\tSoltakh is at Fail-á-Khro, south of Dûn Covád and north of Aughaire. Having slipped the false orders into the Angmarim strongboxes, you should return to Soltakh at Fail-á-Khro.\n",
[5005]="70009984\n1\tPlace false wards (total: 5)\tErchiel has asked you to modify a series of Gauradan-markers into Wards of Doom to prevent the Gauredain from crossing into the Eavespires. The Gauradan-markers are along the river to the north of the Eavespires.\n2\tTalk to Erchiel\tYou should return and tell Erchiel that you have finished placing the wards. Erchiel is at the Eavespires, south of the river.\n",
[5006]="70000056\n1\tDeliver the sack of goods to Ollie Redbrush\tOllie Redbrush is waiting in the armour and weapons shop east of the Bree Town Hall in Bree-town. Falster placed the relics you collected into a sack and bade you deliver them to Ollie Redbrush.\n2\tDeliver the coinpurse to Falster the Fox\tFalster the Fox is in The Forsaken Inn of the Lone-lands, east of Bree. Ollie Redbrush gave you a meagre payment and expressed his displeasure before sending you back to Falster the Fox at The Forsaken Inn.\n",
[5007]="70000057\n1\tBring curiosities to Falster the Fox\030Collect Arnorian heirlooms (total: 5)\030Collect Arnorian coins (total: 5)\030Collect wolf-teeth (total: 10)\tCoins and heirlooms can be found in the Arnorian rubble located in the valley beneath Minas Eriol, south-east of The Forsaken Inn. Wolves also stalk the valley. Falster the Fox, a trader working for a man named Ollie Redbrush, has asked you to collect some old coins and heirlooms for him. Falster wants you to hunt the wolves there for teeth that may help to make up for the delay of his delivery to Ollie Redbrush.\n",
[5008]="70043097\n1\tTravel to the eastern gate of Pelargir\tThe gate into Upper Lebennin can be found in north-eastern Pelargir. Faltharan has asked you to travel into Upper Lebennin and aid him in seeking his lost father. You should travel to the eastern gate.\n2\tTravel to Glaniath in Upper Lebennin\tGlaniath can be found along the road outside the eastern gate of Pelargir. Faltharan has bidden you to meet him at Glaniath, a small farming village in Upper Lebennin. He hopes to begin his search in the surrounding area.\n3\tAsk someone in Glaniath if Faltharan has arrived\tPeople can be found inside Glaniath in Upper Lebennin. You have arrived at Glaniath, but have not yet seen Faltharan. You should ask an inhabitant of Glaniath if they have seen him.\n",
[5009]="7004178E\n1\tSpeak with Faltharan\tFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Faltharan.\n2\tJoin Faltharan as he confronts Lorvegil\tFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Faltharan.\n3\tTalk to Faltharan\tFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Faltharan.\n",
[5010]="70025774\n1\tDiscover what became of Durell\tThe Halls of Night may be found in the hills to the east of Aughaire, beyond the northern gate. Discover what became of Durell in the Halls of Night.\n2\tReturn to Declan with news of his grandfather\tYou have discovered that Shadow is the grandfather of Declan, his spirit trapped for centuries in the Halls of Night.\n",
[5011]="70035293\n1\tFind the memorial dedicated to Alferth\030Light the memorial flame for Gárwig's fallen grandson, Alferth\tThe memorial dedicated to Gárwig's grandson Alferth can be found in the southern Writhendowns. You should light the memorial flame for Alferth to ease the grief of his grandfather.\n2\tFind the memorial dedicated to Wilsig\030Light the memorial flame for Gárwig's grandson, Wilsig\tThe memorial dedicated to Gárwig's grandson Wilsig can be found in the southern Writhendowns. You should light the memorial flame for Wilsig to ease the grief of his grandfather.\n3\tFind the memorial dedicated to Cuthard\030Light the memorial flame for Gárwig's grandson, Cuthard\tThe memorial dedicated to Gárwig's grandson Cuthard can be found in the southern Writhendowns. You should light the memorial flame for Cuthard to ease the grief of his grandfather.\n4\tAssure Gárwig that his grandsons have been honoured\tGárwig is in the Mead Hall Lornsettle in Forlaw. You should return to Gárwig, and offer him the comfort that the flames burn bright in memory of his fallen grandsons.\n",
[5012]="7006225C\n1\tFind Cedrach the Cruel\tHenbran Amon has suggested you retrieve the Amon family grimoire from her sister, Cedrach the Cruel. Cedrach lives in the Old Forest, in Cardolan.\n2\tCollect slippery cap mushrooms (total: 8)\030Collect willow bark (total: 4)\030Collect yarrow (total: 8)\tCedrach Amon has asked you to gather willow bark, yarrow, and slippery cap mushrooms while she searches her cottage for the trunk. You should look for these items in the Old Forest.\n3\tReturn to Cedrach\tYou should bring the yarrow, willow bark, and mushrooms to Cedrach. Cedrach is in the Old Forest.\n",
[5013]="70067F73\n1\tReturn the family necklace to Miritah in Khûtra\030Find the Yâshalam family necklace\tSearch the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo for a heavy, ornate necklace that the Yâshalam family lost. The ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo can be found in the hills east of Khûtra. Then bring it back to the Yâshalam Family Emissary, Miritah.\n",
[5014]="70007584\n1\tBring the heirlooms to Bruner Stoutthrush\030Collect stolen family heirlooms (total: 5)\tThe brigands can be found in a large camp in the Yellow Tree Ruins, south of Staddle; but it may be that some others in the Chetwood also carry stolen items. Whether as an act of beneficence or complete self-interest, Stoutthrush has asked you to collect stolen heirlooms from the brigands and bring them to him at Bree's Combe-gate.\n",
[5015]="70048C9E\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Faltor Gâm (total: 10)\tInfected Orcs can be found in Faltor Gâm, in central Agarnaith. You should defeat Orcs in Faltor Gâm.\n2\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found at Viznak's Hideout. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[5016]="70026F02\n1\tTalk to Séarl in the north-east Dunbog\030Collect toad-legs (total: 5)\tToads are all around the camp-fire where Séarl is encamped in the Dunbog. Séarl has asked you to fetch toad-legs for him.\n",
[5017]="70054F02\n1\tBurn the remains of wights at Aufaltor\tBurn the remains of wights at Aufaltor.\n2\tBurn the remains of wights at Aufaltor (total: 12)\tWights can be found at Aufaltor. You have encountered a number of wights at Aufaltor. You should burn their remains to prevent them from being raised again.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the wights at Aufaltor.\n",
[5018]="70040358\n1\tSpeak with Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth to gain rep.\n",
[5019]="7004035A\n1\tSpeak with Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth to gain rep.\n",
[5020]="7004035B\n1\tSpeak with Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth to gain rep.\n",
[5021]="7004035C\n1\tSpeak with Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth to gain rep.\n",
[5022]="7003EA7B\n1\tSearch Wellinghall for signs of upheaval\030Search the Easeful Mead for signs of upheaval\030Look around from the centre of Derndingle\030Search Derndingle for signs of upheaval\tWellinghall can be found far to the north-west of Derndingle, the Easeful Mead to the north, and Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam has asked you to scout Wellinghall, the Easeful Mead, and Derndingle for signs that the forest has grown wild and angry.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found in Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest. You have searched all of the locations to which Quickbeam directed you, and should now return to him with what you have learned.\n",
[5023]="7002BBD5\n1\tSave Fangorn from Saruman's forces\tDefend Fangorn from the press of Saruman's foul 'industry' and destroy the Wizard's forces there.\n",
[5024]="7002BBD8\n1\tSave Fangorn by destroying Saruman's forces\tWork your way up the side of the hill and to the edge of the Fangorn. Defeat all the enemy forces that stand in your way. Protect the Ents!\n",
})
